      "skill_tags": ["functions", "inverse_functions"],
      "problem_text": "Given $f(x) = \\frac{2x+3}{x-1}$, $x \\neq 1$, find $f^{-1}(x)$.",
      "answer": "$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x+3}{x-2}$, $x \\neq 2$",
      "solution": "Let $y = \\frac{2x+3}{x-1}$. Swap $x$ and $y$: $x = \\frac{2y+3}{y-1}$. Multiply: $x(y-1)=2y+3$, $xy-x=2y+3$, $xy-2y=x+3$, $y(x-2)=x+3$, $y = \\frac{x+3}{x-2}$. So $f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x+3}{x-2}$, $x \\neq 2$"
    },
